# What the image build must not see.
#
# Without this the build works in CI and fails on a developer's machine, which
# is the worst way round. A checkout in CI has no `node_modules`; a checkout
# someone has worked in does, and `COPY apps/web apps/web` then copies pnpm's
# symlink farm over the install the image just did. The links point outside the
# image, so they resolve to nothing, and the build fails claiming a dependency
# is missing that is sitting right there.
#
# It also keeps the context small. Sending a few hundred megabytes of
# `node_modules` and `.venv` to the daemon before anything starts is most of the
# wait on a cold build.

# --- dependency trees, installed inside the image instead --------------------
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
# apps/web/dist is deliberately *not* here: it is built in the image's own web
# stage, and excluding it costs nothing either way. These are the ones that
# would be copied in and shadow something.
apps/desktop/dist
apps/desktop/release
apps/desktop/web
site

# --- things with no business in an image -------------------------------------
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docs
*.md
!apps/api/README.md
